<title>UK: UK's Labour considers Post Office stake sale - paper.</title>
<headline>UK's Labour considers Post Office stake sale - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's opposition Labour Party is considering proposals to sell a major stake in the state-owned Post Office if it wins next month's general election, The Independent newspaper reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper said Labour was examining plans put forward by the Post Office itself to sell a 49 or 51 percent stake, which could raise 2.0 billion pounds ($3.2 billion) towards filling a &quot;black hole' in the party's budget for public finances.</p>
<p>&quot;Labour's deputy leader John Prescott, a strong advocate of partnerships between the private and public sector, has been briefed on the plans by John Roberts, chief executive of the Post Office,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 1717 542 7717</p>
<p>($ = 0.615 British Pounds)</p>
